		\entry{Independent Advanced Study}{2025 -- Present}
		\item[] Self-study of graduate-level texts to bridge the gap between undergraduate topology and current research:
		\begin{itemize}[label=\textperiodcentered]
			\item \textbf{B. Farb \& D. Margalit, \textit{A Primer on Mapping Class Groups}:} Surface homeomorphisms, Dehn twists and braid groups (preparation for Copenhagen).
			\item \textbf{J. Munkres, \textit{Topology} \& \textit{Elements of Algebraic Topology}:} Fundamental groups and covering spaces; currently studying singular homology.
			\item \textbf{S. Kalajdzievski, \textit{An Illustrated Introduction to Topology and Homology}:} Visualization techniques for higher-dimensional structures.
		\end{itemize}
	\end{itemize}
	
